      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Type 2 diabetes is associated with increased risk of malignancies, whereas antidiabetic interventions like physical exercise or metformin reduce cancer incidence. A recent publication shows that one diabetes treatment approach, namely incretin-related DPP4 inhibitors, increases metastatic capacity by activating the antioxidant transcription factor NRF2 to decrease reactive oxygen species (ROS) levels."
      },
